  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Homeowners insurance in Utah covers a roof leak only if the damage results from a sudden, accidental event like a severe windstorm, hail, or a fallen tree branch.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "Homeowners insurance in Utah covers a roof leak only if the damage results from a sudden, accidental event like a severe windstorm, hail, or a fallen tree branch"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "What Is Covered"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Storm Damage: Leaks caused directly by wind tearing off shingles, heavy hail impact, or lightning."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Interior Water Damage: Ruined drywall, ceilings, or flooring caused by a storm-related roof breach."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Falling Objects: Leaks caused by tree branches crashing through the roof."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "What Is NOT Covered"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Wear and Tear: Leaks caused by an aging roof or old, deteriorated shingles."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Neglect and Maintenance: Leaks from issues you delayed fixing, rotted decking, or poor original installation."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Floods: Rising surface water requires separate flood insurance, which standard policies exclude."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "What to Do Next"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Prevent more damage: Safely use a tarp to cover holes and move electronics or furniture away from the drip zone."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Document everything: Take clear photos and videos of both the exterior roof problem and the interior water damage before starting any cleanup."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Review your policy: Check your specific deductible and coverage limits, as filing a claim makes sense only if the repair cost exceeds your deductible. You can read more about local guidelines on the Logan Roof Pros Blog or check resources for Roof Leak Repair in Utah .",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "Logan Roof Pros Blog",
                "link": "https://www.loganroofpros.com/blog/will-home-insurance-cover-roof-leak/"
              },
              {
                "text": "Roof Leak Repair in Utah",
                "link": "https://skyridgeco.com/roof-leak-repair-utah-2026"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you want, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What the leak (a recent storm, aging shingles, etc.)?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "How bad is the interior water damage?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you figure out your next steps or what to tell your insurance adjuster."
      }
    ],
